      "text": "21 Charles Sanders Peirce, “The Fixation of Belief” (1877) and “How to Make Our Ideas\nClear” (1878), in The Essential Peirce, vol. 1 (Bloomington: Indiana University Press, 1992),\nwhere truth is understood as the hypothesis that inquiry rationally converges upon because it\nbest explains the available evidence under continued testing.\n                                42",
