      "text": "Reason, Revelation and the Architecture of Truth\n    •   Christian canon containing falsely attributed writings.\n\nTable 5.1\n Preservation Axis Comparison Across Major Scriptures\n\n                                             Mass                             Liturgical\n                    Original        Text\n                                            memorization of   Oral + written      use in\n   Scripture       language      unchanged\n                                                   the entire       transmission?      original\n                   preserved?       globally?\n                                                  corpus?                         language?\n\n Hebrew         Partially,       No, MT,    No               Limited         Yes\n Bible /       Hebrew       LXX, SP,\n Pentateuch     preserved, but  DSS\n                 vocalization      plurality.\n                     later; Aramaic\n                  sections exist.\n\n Christian    No         No        No          No             Rare\n Bible\n\n Vedas         Yes         No           Yes (partial,         Partially         Limited\n                  (recensional)                    lineage-based\n\n Buddhist    No         No        No (except          Partially (early    Monastic\n Canon                                      monastic             oral, later        only\n                                                    subsets)            written)\n\n Qurʾān        Yes             Yes           Yes               Yes             Yes\n\n   On this axis, the Qurʾān uniquely satisfies the criteria of coherent authorship,\nabsence of pseudepigrapha, and historically stable transmission—bringing its\ninternal claims into direct correspondence with a publicly recoverable and testable\nexternal manuscript record.66",
