      "text": " Philosophical Tradition /\n                                Epistemic Axis               Core Limitation\n      Key Thinkers\nChristian Scholasticism       Christian-Aristotelian        Faith subsumes reason under ecclesiastical\n(Augustine, Aquinas)        metaphysical synthesis        authority; revelation monopolized, and\n                                                         truth mediated through dogma;\n                                                             overreliance on metaphysical syllogisms\n                                                         detaches inquiry from empirical reality.\nRationalism (Descartes,    A priori reason and logical    Overreliance on internal reason; assumes\nSpinoza, Leibniz)           deduction                   the mind as self-validating, creating\n                                                          epistemic circularity and detachment\n                                                 from empirical reality.\nEmpiricism (Bacon, Locke,   Sensory observation and      Overreliance on sensory data. Cannot\nHume)                     induction                       justify induction or universal moral\n                                                               truths; experience is contingent and\n                                                             unstable.\nKantian Transcendentalism  Mind’s structuring forms and Constrains knowledge to phenomena; the\n                               categories of understanding  noumena remains unknowable, leaving\n                                                                    reality partly inaccessible.\nHegelian Idealism            Historical dialectic of Spirit   Self-enclosed system lacking external\n                               (Geist)                         calibration; tends toward conceptual\n                                                 monism.\nPositivism / Scientism       Empirical verification and    Reduces truth to what is measurable;\n(Comte, Carnap, Russell,     quantitative measurement    tends to treat consciousness as an\nWittgenstein)                                         “emergent property;” excludes\n                                                       metaphysics and moral meaning as “non-\n                                                             empirical.”\nWittgenstein / Language     Language-games and        Meaning becomes usage-bound within\nPhilosophy                  contextual meaning          language-games; truth is suspended\n                                                 beyond shared social practice.\n                                                     Normativity is treated as arising from\n                                                             practice itself, leaving moral authority\n                                                                    self-referential and epistemically\n                                                   ungrounded.",
