      "text": "6:141, 17:26, 30:38.\nits / his due\n\nvi. ḥaqqun\n3:86, 10:53, 10:53, 10:55, 18:21, 28:13, 30:60, 31:33, 35:5, \n38:64, 40:55, 40:77, 45:32, 46:17, 51:23, 56:95, 69:51.\ntrue, truth\n\nvii. ḥaqqin\nbi ḥaqqin\n5:116.\n\nThe preposition bi is a function of the verb laisa in this case and \none of the ways it takes an object.\n\n(a) right\nmin ḥaqqin (fi)\n11:79.\nDictionary definition of ḥaqq fī: a right to.\nviii. ḥaqqun + li\n51:19, 70:24-25\na due for\nix. ḥaqqa + ʿalā\n7:30.\n\ndue upon\n\nbil ḥaqqi\nThis convention occurs a total of 76 times. The core distinction \nto be made is between those cases where:\n\n•\t bi is the preposition which the verb uses to engage an object: \ngenerally, (with) the truth\n•\t bi is not a preposition needed by the verb to engage an \nobject, but operating together with al ḥaqq to produce an \nindependent adverbial phrase: generally, by right.\n\nThe full set of instances for bil ḥaqqi is:",
