      "title": "Addenda to The Qur’an: A Complete Revelation — Sam Gerrans",
      "section": "Shayṭān, Jinn, and Related Terms Considered [PDF p. 60]",
      "section_number": 59,
      "chunk_number": 0,
      "source_path": "research/articles/sam-gerrans-addenda-to-the-quran-a-complete-revelation.md",
      "verse_refs": [
        "37:158"
      ],
      "topics": [],
      "text": "forces — comprises in total invisible forces of two types: those \nwith individual, malevolent will (satans), and those with no \nindividual will (the underlying forces driving the operating \nsystem of the Matrix).\nThus, when the Qur’an states that al jinna /  الجِنَّةare destined \nfor Hell, this references both the damned condition of the satans \nand the temporary nature of the underlying operating system \nupon which this dunyā (or temporary life) rests and depends.\n\nThis brings us to the last verse which contains al jinna / .الجِنَّة\n\n158 And they have made between Him and the jinna a \nkinship — when the jinna know they will be summoned.\n(37:158)\n\nThe term in question could be understood here in both its \ngeneral applications.",
      "source_kind": "attributed_external_research",
      "evidence_role": "argument_not_scripture",
      "external_discussion": true,
      "author": "Sam Gerrans",
      "pdf_page": 60
